cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or empirical data in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "An Empirical Evaluation of Threshold Sensitivity and Calibration Transfer in Benign-Trained Network Anomaly Detection"
authors:
  - family-names: "Shukla"
    given-names: "Skand"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Skand203/benign-calibrated-nids"
abstract: "This repository provides the complete experimental code, statistical analysis pipelines, and evaluation outputs for an empirical investigation into benign-trained anomaly detection on the UNSW-NB15 benchmark. The research evaluates Isolation Forest, Local Outlier Factor (LOF), and One-Class SVM, focusing on calibration transfer stability, threat heterogeneity, and benchmark structural artifacts."
keywords:
  - "network intrusion detection"
  - "anomaly detection"
  - "threshold calibration"
  - "calibration transfer"
  - "UNSW-NB15"
  - "local outlier factor"
  - "isolation forest"
  - "one-class SVM"
date-released: 2026-11-17
version: "1.0.0"
type: "software"
